      "writtenOn": "2022-12-12T14:22:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like we are going out of our way not to define `AtomicType::hasAtomicMember` as true. Is it in some way beneficial that \"has atomic member\" returns `false` for a plain/unwrapped atomic type?\n\nContrast with `Type::isOrContainsArray` and `Type::isOrContainsUnsizedArray`--these helpers return true if you have an array, _or_ if you have a struct with an array nested inside. It seems like that pattern makes it easier on callers, and is just as easy to implement. I don\u0027t feel strongly about it per se, and if `hasAtomicMember` returning false for a plain `atomicUint` is making things easier elsewhere, that SGTM. Just trying to noodle through the rationale for this pattern.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 158,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 158,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "d5806eea0f675d9fcac42397848e93224cf1fc3a",
